## Workflow (agentkit)

Every feature goes spec → tests → freeze → implement. Phases (`status:` in `spec.md`):
`draft` → `approved` → `tests-draft` → `tests-approved` → `frozen` → `done`.

**Session start:** read the resume point printed by `status` (or the last section of
`{{specs}}/README.md`), then only the active spec's `progress.md`. Work on one phase of one
spec per session. Only `kickoff` and `feature` assign spec numbers.

### Hard rules
1. Frozen files never change: no edit, move, delete or regeneration, by any tool or shell
   command. If a frozen test looks wrong, stop and tell the owner. Only the owner unfreezes.
2. Never edit `{{lock}}`, `{{unfreeze_log}}`, `{{chaos_log}}`, `{{specs}}/*/reviews/`,
   `agentkit.toml` or `.agentkit/`. Never commit with `--no-verify`, change `core.hooksPath`,
   or run `lock unfreeze` or `chaos clear`.
3. The owner owns the gates. Set `approved`, `tests-approved` or `dropped` only when the owner
   said so in this conversation. `frozen` is set only by `lock freeze`. Where chaos mode
   applies, gates go through `agentkit chaos approve`.
4. Make tests pass honestly: no special-casing of test inputs, no skipped or weakened checks.
5. Every test name starts with the requirement ID it covers.

### Commands
| Need | Command |
|---|---|
| Full suite (compact summary) | `{{python}} .agentkit/bin/agentkit test` |
| One module or test | `{{python}} .agentkit/bin/agentkit test <scope>` |
| Where code lives | `{{codemap}}` (refresh: `{{python}} .agentkit/bin/agentkit codemap`) |
| Requirement coverage | `{{python}} .agentkit/bin/agentkit trace --spec NNN` |
| Lock check | `{{python}} .agentkit/bin/agentkit lock verify` |

### Token discipline
- Read the spec's API contract and `tasks.md` first. Open only the files they point to.
- Run targeted tests while working and the full suite before each commit.
- Hand verbose work (wide searches, long logs) to a fast-tier subagent.
- Commits: `spec(NNN): …`, `test(NNN): …`, `feat(NNN): …`, `fix: …`, `docs: …`.
